<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Results" id="results1">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1500" pageHeight="1850" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="title" value="Real-Data Backtest Results: REAL Dispatch vs. TRAINED Model (Cycle-Based)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="20" width="1380" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="1,667 real historical orders, 42 real drivers -- TRAINED's candidate pool limited to the SAME 42 drivers REAL used. A CYCLE = one full loop, home base to home base -- see glossary below." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontStyle=2;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="58" width="1380" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>


        <mxCell id="model_banner" value="Model: state_value_function_v4_hours_since_home.pkl (documents/logs/27) -- NOW the deployed live model (dashboard/server/main.py, sim/live/score_quote.py), swapped in on the user's explicit call after this backtest picture and the disclosed paired-comparison revenue tradeoff were both weighed. Numbers below were corrected THREE TIMES after direct, sustained user pushback (&quot;something is off&quot;) surfaced four real bugs: REAL not judged by the same idle-timeout standard as TRAINED, TRAINED's own undercounting bug, empty-miles only pricing the cycle-closing leg, and TRAINED's cycle reconstruction dropping the 130 recovered orders it's credited for elsewhere -- plus a real RNG non-determinism bug. All fixed; see documents/logs/27's follow-ups." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FCE4CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="84" width="1380" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <!-- ===== Glossary ===== -->
        <mxCell id="gloss_hdr" value="How to Read These Results: What a &quot;Cycle&quot; Is" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="130" width="1380" height="35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gloss_body" value="&#8226; CYCLE: one full loop for a driver -- leaving home base, working a sequence of real trips, and returning to home base. Every cycle is closed one of three ways; there is no &quot;incomplete, excluded&quot; case.&#xa;&#8226; Closed by a real paid trip: a real order's own destination happens to BE the driver's home hub -- 0 empty miles, the trip itself completed the return.&#xa;&#8226; Closed by a real SIMULATED deadhead leg (BOTH arms): whenever a driver goes idle without a next job lined up, the SAME repositioning_outcome() decision (documents/logs/25-27) checks every 24h whether they'd reposition -- toward their own home hub once real urgency justifies it, otherwise the nearest hub -- priced as a real empty distance, not a guess. REAL was NOT held to this standard until a direct user correction caught the asymmetry (documents/logs/27 follow-up): REAL's own idle gaps are now judged by the identical rule TRAINED's IDLE_TIMEOUT mechanism already was.&#xa;&#8226; Closed by an ASSUMED empty return (&quot;no trip&quot;): the driver is still not observed back at home base by the time the whole replay window runs out -- that remaining gap to home IS the empty-return-miles metric, priced at real routed distance. This is now the RARE case for both arms (the idle-timeout check above handles most mid-window gaps); it only fires for whatever's left at the very end.&#xa;&#8226; HOS remaining at return: legal driving/duty hours still available but UNUSED once back home -- real forgone capacity. Reconstructed for REAL from the SAME seeded starting HOS condition TRAINED's own simulated fleet uses (identical random seed), walked forward through REAL's own actual pickup/delivery timestamps -- a real reconstruction, not an assumption about REAL.&#xa;&#8226; These 42 real drivers home to a genuinely DIVERSE mix -- 31 Milton, 7 Barrie, 4 London (fixed earlier this session: an old version of this analysis incorrectly showed all 42 as London-only, before calibration.driver_home_hub existed -- see sim/calibrate_driver_home_hub.py).&#xa;&#8226; Empty-return-miles is a RUNNING TOTAL across the WHOLE cycle (fixed same day, documents/logs/27 follow-up: an earlier version only counted the cycle-CLOSING leg, silently missing the far more common ordinary deadhead between consecutive trips within a cycle, for both arms)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CCCCCC;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=15;spacingTop=12;spacingRight=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="167" width="1380" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

