        <mxCell id="panelB_note" value="THREE TIMES corrected (documents/logs/27 follow-ups, all from direct, sustained user pushback -- real bugs, not reassurances): (1) REAL wasn't judged by the same idle-timeout standard as TRAINED; (2) empty miles only counted the cycle-CLOSING leg, not the whole cycle, for both arms; (3) TRAINED's own cycle reconstruction silently DROPPED all 130 recovered orders, even though the driver's real decisions were made with them available and every other panel here credits TRAINED for them -- fixed, plus a real RNG non-determinism bug (Python's hash() on a tuple was randomized per-process, causing REAL's own cycle count to drift between reruns: 763/764/770/770 -- fixed with a stable integer seed, now byte-identical across reruns, confirmed directly). With all fixes in: TRAINED's total cycle revenue now reconciles exactly to its own known aggregate ($242,868 vs the $243,277 reported elsewhere). Revenue/trips per cycle are STILL lower for TRAINED -- genuinely, not a bug -- because TRAINED earns MORE total revenue across EVEN MORE cycles (1,094 vs REAL's 770): more, shorter loops home, the direct signature of prioritizing driver-home-time, independently confirmed by the paired-comparison test's real revenue cost (p=0.0188). Empty miles, HOS margin, and cycle duration all favor TRAINED. This model (v4) IS the deployed live model (documents/logs/27) -- deployed on that explicit, disclosed tradeoff." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="895" width="1380" height="85" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

